+### Reusing untimed benchmark inputs
+
+The private-opening and range-opening benchmarks accept `BENCH_FIXTURE_DIR`
+for optional immutable setup caches. Each cache key includes the executable
+hash and all input parameters; a complete-file checksum is verified before
+loading. Partial writes are ignored, and a damaged completed fixture fails
+the run. Public range fixtures include primary columns, auxiliary rows and
+the trusted root. Private fixtures preserve the bulk builder's append state,
+so each process restores its own mutable baseline. No measured operation,
+PIR hint or response-packing table is cached. The publication artifact sets
+this directory inside the run so adaptive batches and range helper/client
+jobs can share their identical setup.
+
+The private-client benchmark builds only the records touched by its opening,
+including records holding the upper nodes. Its replies, corruption cases and
+client timers are unchanged. The materialized-opening baseline uses the same
+tiled dense builder and compact packing preprocessing as TreePIR, with an
+independent bitwise reference packer and checked replies. See the
+[comparison documentation](documentation/treepir-ypir.md#the-artifact-comparison)
+for independent sampling groups and server warmups. Public range
+helper timings similarly average 32 calls per independent sample, preserving
+response destruction inside their existing timing boundary.
+
 ### Compile-only benchmark check
 ```bash
 cargo check --features bench --benches
